# CardDemo frontend environment template.
#
# Copy this file to frontend/.env.local before building or running the frontend.
# From the repository root:
#
#     cp frontend/.env.local.example frontend/.env.local
#
# The copy is git-ignored, so local edits never reach the repository.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL is the backend origin: scheme, host and port, with no path.
# Do not add /api/v1; the API client (src/lib/apiClient.ts) appends it to every call.
#
# Next.js inlines NEXT_PUBLIC_* values into the browser bundle when npm run build runs.
# Changing the value therefore requires a rebuild; restarting the server is not enough.
#
# Use the host 127.0.0.1, never localhost. The session cookie is SameSite=Lax, and a
# browser treats localhost and 127.0.0.1 as different sites, so a page served from one
# would not send the cookie to an API on the other. Serve the frontend from the same
# host: its origin, http://127.0.0.1:3000, is the value of BACKEND_CORS_ORIGINS in
# backend/.env.
#
# The value is public: it ships to every browser, so it must never carry a secret.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000
